WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:09.009 --> 00:00:10.051
Somehow these

00:00:10.051 --> 00:00:13.555
elephants are eking out
a living in a landscape

00:00:14.055 --> 00:00:16.057
that anyone else would think is lifeless.

00:00:19.310 --> 00:00:20.770
Conservationist Dr.

00:00:20.770 --> 00:00:26.109
Paula Kahumbu has spent her career
studying the elephants of Africa's lush

00:00:26.109 --> 00:00:31.614
savanna grasslands.

00:00:31.614 --> 00:00:36.411
But she's never laid
eyes on a desert elephant.

00:00:36.911 --> 00:00:40.123
She wants to find out
how these remarkable animals

00:00:40.290 --> 00:00:46.337
managed to survive
in this unforgiving place.

00:00:46.337 --> 00:00:50.258
African savanna elephants and desert
elephants are the same species.

00:00:50.800 --> 00:00:54.137
But if you took a savanna elephant
and brought it here, it wouldn't survive.

00:00:55.346 --> 00:00:57.682
I want to know how these desert elephants

00:00:57.932 --> 00:01:01.019
managed to live here.

00:01:04.522 --> 00:01:07.484
To find one of the constantly roaming
elephant herds,

00:01:08.068 --> 00:01:10.862
Paula has turned to tracker
Hendrik Moon in Bomi

00:01:11.446 --> 00:01:14.699
and his 25 years of studying
the Desert Elephant.

00:01:15.742 --> 00:01:18.495
I think some walk through a soft

00:01:20.872 --> 00:01:22.624
so it's possible

00:01:22.624 --> 00:01:24.709
we’ll find them today.

00:01:45.396 --> 00:01:55.365
Oh, this amazing

00:01:57.283 --> 00:01:58.701
there’s two here.

00:01:58.701 --> 00:02:01.204
Oh, you mean theres a big family here.

00:02:01.246 --> 00:02:01.913
Yeah.

00:02:02.205 --> 00:02:04.624
These are the desert elephants
we've been looking for.

00:02:05.792 --> 00:02:11.172
This family.

00:02:11.172 --> 00:02:13.508
I've been watching elephants
my whole life,

00:02:13.716 --> 00:02:16.219
and I've never seen elephants like these.

00:02:17.512 --> 00:02:20.265
They may be the same species
as savanna elephants,

00:02:20.431 --> 00:02:22.517
but you can immediately
see the differences.

00:02:23.560 --> 00:02:26.271
The legs have less fat in them,
so they look taller

00:02:27.063 --> 00:02:29.357
and their skin is looser.

00:02:29.357 --> 00:02:31.526
It's incredibly tough for an elephant
here.

00:02:32.777 --> 00:02:34.779
Food and water are both scarce

00:02:35.864 --> 00:02:38.408
and it's only getting worse

00:02:38.408 --> 00:02:39.826
in the Namib desert.

00:02:39.826 --> 00:02:42.579
Climate change has brought with it
a five year drought.

00:02:44.581 --> 00:02:46.666
Everything depends on their ability

00:02:46.875 --> 00:02:50.128
to get from one waterhole to the next.

00:02:51.629 --> 00:02:53.798
There's no time to stop,

00:02:53.798 --> 00:02:56.968
to investigate, to explore how to play.

00:02:58.178 --> 00:03:00.471
It's just survive.

00:03:00.555 --> 00:03:02.265
Survive means keep going.

00:03:02.265 --> 00:03:13.109
Keep going.

